1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,622
Three charts. Three new skills to test.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:04,505
Gaps, plans and support.

3
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:08,158
Question one. Earnings came out, and the stock gapped up.

4
00:00:08,506 --> 00:00:10,624
Will the gap fill, or will it gap and go?

5
00:00:14,474 --> 00:00:15,183
It filled.

6
00:00:15,591 --> 00:00:24,509
Volume faded after the open, and long upper wicks showed sellers waiting above. Gaps on strong, rising volume are more likely to keep going.

7
00:00:25,009 --> 00:00:29,994
Question two. Same entry, two plans. Green is the target, red is the stop.

8
00:00:30,332 --> 00:00:31,979
Is plan A better, or plan B?

9
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:36,536
Plan B.

10
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:44,797
Plan A risks as much as it can make. Plan B risks a little to make several times more. You can be wrong more often, and still come out ahead.

11
00:00:45,297 --> 00:00:49,643
Question three. Price is falling again, with three lines drawn underneath.

12
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:52,533
Which one is real support? A, B, or C?

13
00:00:56,383 --> 00:00:56,880
B.

14
00:00:57,217 --> 00:01:03,948
Buyers stepped in at that level three times before, so traders are watching it. A and C are just lines on a chart.

15
00:01:04,448 --> 00:01:07,192
How many did you get? Tell me your score in the comments.

16
00:01:07,582 --> 00:01:11,214
Practise on real charts from the game, at memestreet.net.

